Z||000001||AusFiero||07-26-2001||12:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Just wondering because over here most of the real riced up vehicles are owned by young Turkish and Lebanese trouble makers who are usually in clubs resembling gangs not car clubs. Most come to our hometown from Sydney Sunday afternoons and cause nothing but trouble. Roads get closed, carparks cordenned off just trying to get them to stay away. Spoils many a weekend for locals and tourists alike. We don't need Sydneys trash on the coast. They have no respect for anyone or anything when here and just trash what they can then drive back to Sydney to Bankstown mostly where they then participate in Autralias only area of drive by shootings and gang violence and such. <P>Don't take that as racism please but it is an observation that many Aussies would back up. I have nothing against any race/colour/creed when people try to get along but for some reason these are the people that have these cars here. The really really really riced up ones.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>OOPS I thought I had posted this in off topic. Nice pic of my Fiero below huh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||07-26-2001||01:25 PM||||I can only speak for places I have been, which is mainly Baltimore and the surrounding states (also went to Nopi nationals once), mainly asians under 25 yrs. of age.  However there are a lot of suburbia white kids that are up and coming.  I mean, lets face it, what 17 year old kid can afford a $15-20k dollar Acura Integra, plus a $1k body kit with installation, 17" rims etc. etc. etc.  They can't, mommy and daddy can though.  There is a local hangout where a lot of them go almost every night, I went up there once with a friend who knows some of them, out of about 15 cars, Eclipses Integras Civics etc., only 1 kid paid for his and it was a 1st gen. Eclipse.  All the others got theirs for their 16th or 17th birthdays.  Must be nice.<BR> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||07-26-2001||02:45 PM||||Yeah, that's pretty much what it is here in NJ. But it's not just white kids here. it's all the 16-19 year old punk kids that dont' care about anything because mommy and daddy can buy them out of trouble.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroKyle||07-26-2001||02:57 PM||||Usually people under 29. It can be anyone, but the rarest of ricers I see is a Black guy. They just put rims on and lower the car usually. Also they load it up with speakers. But thats about it. I think anyways. Saw a riced up Malibu today. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Justin||07-26-2001||03:06 PM||||Some kid I know has been working for the past 3 years, and he works pretty hard too.  But he just spends his money on drugs and stuff.  His 16th birthday came and guess what?  Mommy bought him a brand new Volkwagen Jetta VR6, with leather and everything.  A few weeks later, he backs it into a van and does over $1,000 of damage.  Guess who pays for it?  Mommy.  It aggrevates me.  Mommy in this case is screwing up the kids life.  Unless she plans on paying for everything for the rest of his life, one day she will proably stop buying everything for him and he's gonna be outa luck.  No money, and he won't know how to save money either.  She is just ruining his life basically.  He needs to learn responsibility.  And people don't take care of there cars if the parents buy them, they know it was free.  You can only truly respect your car and take care of it if you pay for it, otherwise it's just a toy, no precautions to take.<P>I have to pay for every penny of my first car, including the car, insurance, tax, title, tags, damage done (hopefully none  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)etc...<P>And speaking of that, does anyone have a car for sale in South Eastern PA?<P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<P>visit <A HREF="http://www.twinkiesproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twinkiesproject.com</A>  for information on the chemical properties, reactions, gravitational resonse, and density issues of a Twinkie.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTBro||07-26-2001||03:07 PM||||Most of the ricers around my area are driven by Philipino kids and some hispanics.  I live in an area that has a high population of Hispanics, so you see a lot of lowriders...  and only some ricers...  Most of the population drives mustangs.  There are several Mustang clubs about.  You can find parking lots full of about 15-20 mustangs on Friday nights with the kids just hanging out.  Then they go off into the country and race until the cops break up the party.<P>Since the economy is so weak in this area... there are no "true" ricers like you see on "The Fast and The Furious"  You only see stock civics and preludes with fart can exhausts.  Not much competition when you challenge them.<P>All the fast cars here are tricked out Mustangs and T/A's<P>BTW..  I live in South Texas about 10 miles from Mexico...<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierobear||07-26-2001||03:24 PM||||Rice boys.||||reg||1
Z||000008||West Coast Fiero||07-26-2001||03:51 PM||||out here in L.A. you will find mainly asain kids with riced out cars, with the occasional black guy and white guy trying to fit in. It is mainly mustangs ( rust-stains ) out here though. But you will see damned near anything at the street races||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||07-26-2001||04:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>Usually people under 29. It can be anyone, but the rarest of ricers I see is a Black guy. They just put rims on and lower the car usually. Also they load it up with speakers. But thats about it. I think anyways. Saw a riced up Malibu today. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, here in central NC, there's a difference between the typical Black dude's car and white/Asian dude's car.  The black man's car is "pimped" instead of "riced", meaning huge wheels and tires - sometimes sticking WAY outside the wheelwells with obscene offsets on the rims. And a mondo uber-stereo.  Don't forget the gold body emblems, too.  Near as I can tell, pimping a car has nothing to do with performance, whereas ricing at least wants to have the LOOK of performance.  Pimped cars are usually driven much more sedately, too.  They want to be seen - not try to show how fast they are.  It's a different attitude altogether.||||reg||1
